Z||000016||Patrick's Dad||11-05-2001||09:57 AM||||Finding things that involve not only too much money, but too much time to complete....<P>The Fiero, of course, is being disaasembled.<P>The telescope (5" Celestron SCT on GEM) is assembled, but I'm lusting after another (4" Televue APO refractor), which is perfect for city astronomy (Cliff...?)<P>The hifi is OK (Paradigm M7's powered by an Adcom 200wpc Amp, Van Alstine tube preamp) but I'd like to convince my wife to get a DVD player (one with a good audio section) so I can move the CD player to:<P>Photography - my darkroom. Still under construction. I did trade much of my Minolta Maxxum gear for a Leica M6TTL and 35 f2ASPH. Also have a 4x5 SpeedGraphic, two 4x5 pinhole cameras (building another one- 1000mm), and a couple of other esoteric cameras.<P>That's it. I'm not allowed any others, unless I'm willing to give up one of these. I could always rebuild my bicycle, which I have all the parts for, but gave up because of asthma....||||reg||12
